1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:03,170
“At night I feel someone is in the room with me,”

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,890
“whenever I hear the Qur’an my whole body feels heavy,”

3
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,860
“I see dreams that frighten me.”

4
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:15,990
Phrases practitioners hear often, and behind them all one question: is there a jinn in my body?

5
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:20,690
Today we pause with the Qur’an, the Sunnah and the experience of scholars of ruqyah,

6
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:26,050
does a jinn enter a human body at all? What signs do practitioners mention?

7
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:31,530
What must we never believe? And what is the lawful path of treatment?

8
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:36,010
Does a jinn enter the human body? Allah says of those who consume usury:

9
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:42,600
“Those who consume usury will not stand except as one stands who is driven to madness by the touch of the devil.”

10
00:00:42,690 --> 00:00:48,160
And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “The devil flows through the son of Adam as blood flows.”

11
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:53,740
Most scholars of Ahl al-Sunnah hold this: a jinn may harm a person and enter his body.

12
00:00:53,830 --> 00:01:00,270
Imam Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal was told: some people say a jinn does not enter a human body,

13
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:04,100
and he said: “They are lying; there he is, speaking on his tongue.”

14
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:09,110
But the same scholars affirmed that this happens only by Allah’s permission,

15
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:17,750
and that the devil has no authority over a servant protected by remembering his Lord. Allah says: “Over My servants you have no authority.”

16
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:25,460
Signs in sleep: practitioners, among them Shaykh Waḥīd ʿAbd al-Salām Bālī in his books, mention signs in the sleep of one harmed by jinn:

17
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:30,310
insomnia and waking often at night, anxiety and fear at bedtime,

18
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:37,930
recurring nightmares, especially seeing cats, dogs, snakes or camels, or frightening animals attacking the sleeper,

19
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:44,390
seeing oneself fall from a height, and seeing graveyards, ruins or dark endless roads,

20
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:49,080
and talking, laughing or screaming in sleep, and sleepwalking.

21
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:51,130
And signs while awake:

22
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,000
sudden tightness and aversion on hearing the adhan or the Qur’an,

23
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,200
sudden intense anger unlike the person’s nature,

24
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,600
a scattered mind and much forgetfulness,

25
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,450
heaviness and numbness in a limb that changes with dhikr,

26
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:12,030
feeling someone is present, especially when alone, and drifting from prayer and worship without knowing why.

27
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:18,730
And signs during ruqyah: practitioners say the most important signs appear on hearing the ruqyah:

28
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:23,910
shivers or trembling in the body, numbness or heaviness in the hands and feet,

29
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:30,460
involuntary crying or laughing, screaming, and in more severe cases, speaking in another voice.

30
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:39,060
But know that yawning, tears or shivers alone are not proof of a jinn; they may simply be the Qur’an’s effect on the heart.

31
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:46,460
And here is the most important point: not every condition is possession, and none of these signs alone is conclusive.

32
00:02:46,550 --> 00:02:54,220
Nightmares, insomnia, anger and sadness have many causes, and blaming every state on jinn wrongs oneself.

33
00:02:54,310 --> 00:03:03,270
In Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī, a Black woman came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: “I have fits, and I become uncovered, so pray to Allah for me.”

34
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:08,600
He said: “If you wish, be patient and Paradise is yours; or if you wish, I will pray to Allah to cure you.”

35
00:03:08,690 --> 00:03:13,480
She said: “I will be patient, but pray to Allah that I don’t become uncovered,” and he prayed for her.

36
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:20,690
Reflect: the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not tell her “this is so-and-so’s doing”; he pointed her to patience, prayer and Paradise.

37
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:26,100
Three things never to believe. First: don’t believe what the jinn says.

38
00:03:26,190 --> 00:03:36,110
Sometimes during ruqyah someone speaks in another voice and says: “So-and-so did sorcery,” or “her mother-in-law sent me,” or “the sorcery is buried in such a place.”

39
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,230
Don’t believe any of it.

40
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:45,010
When the devil taught Abū Hurayra Āyat al-Kursī, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “He told you the truth, though he is a liar.”

41
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:49,140
If the devil is a liar, how can we accuse a family on his word?

42
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:52,620
Second: beating and choking are not ruqyah.

43
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:59,960
Some beat the patient in the name of expelling the jinn, press on his neck, or burn him, and none of this is from the Sunnah.

44
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:07,790
The Prophet’s ruqyah (peace be upon him) was Qur’an, prayer, gentle blowing and wiping with the hand, not beating or harm.

45
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:13,100
A blow that lands on the patient lands on the person’s own body, not on the jinn.

46
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:20,510
Third: being alone with or touching an unrelated woman; no practitioner may be alone with an unrelated woman or touch her body.

47
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:26,320
A woman’s ruqyah is done with her maḥram present, fully covered, and without touch,

48
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:30,940
and whoever doesn’t keep these limits is no practitioner; so get up and leave.

49
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:33,520
The best practitioner for you: you.

50
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:44,880
The Prophet (peace be upon him) said of the seventy thousand who enter Paradise without reckoning: “They are those who do not ask for ruqyah, do not believe in bad omens, and rely upon their Lord.”

51
00:04:44,970 --> 00:04:47,540
That is, they don’t ask others for ruqyah.

52
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:55,430
So the best is to do ruqyah for yourself; you are closer to Allah than you think, and the Qur’an was revealed for you too.

53
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,800
Here is the plan for self-ruqyah: make wudūʾ,

54
00:04:58,890 --> 00:05:05,750
sit facing the qibla, put your right hand on your chest or on the place of pain, and recite: al-Fātiḥa,

55
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:10,050
Āyat al-Kursī, the beginning and the end of Sūrat al-Baqara,

56
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:15,380
verses fifty-four to fifty-six of Sūrat al-Aʿrāf,

57
00:05:15,470 --> 00:05:23,010
from verse one hundred and fifteen to the end of Sūrat al-Muʾminūn, and the start of Sūrat al-Ṣāffāt to verse ten,

58
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:27,370
and al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq and an-Nās, three times each.

59
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:31,980
After each sura, blow gently into your hands and wipe your body with them.

60
00:05:32,070 --> 00:05:35,630
Recite the same verses over water, then drink from it and wash with it.

61
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:42,770
And recite Sūrat al-Baqara in your home, for he (peace be upon him) told us the devil flees from the house in which it is recited.

62
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:50,700
Doors that must stay closed: the Prophet (peace be upon him) showed us doors we should close:

63
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:54,760
When angry, say: “I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed devil,”

64
00:05:54,850 --> 00:06:00,840
for he (peace be upon him) said of an angry man: “If he said it, what he feels would leave him.”

65
00:06:00,930 --> 00:06:08,700
When yawning, cover your mouth; he (peace be upon him) said: “Let him hold his hand over his mouth, for the devil enters.”

66
00:06:08,790 --> 00:06:14,210
On entering the toilet, say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils.”

67
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:20,950
Morning and evening, don’t leave the adhkār, and say a hundred times a day, as a protection until evening:

68
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:28,430
“There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His the praise, and He is capable of all things.”

69
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:31,770
So if you ask: how do I know there is a jinn in my body?

70
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:36,510
Know the signs but don’t judge by them, don’t believe what the jinn says,

71
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:42,170
don’t count anyone who beats or violates boundaries as a practitioner, and begin ruqyah yourself,

72
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:47,370
certain of Allah’s words: “Indeed, the plot of the devil is ever weak.”

73
00:06:47,450 --> 00:06:54,390
Send this clip to someone living with this fear, and write in the comments: “O Allah, protect us from the devils among jinn and men.”

74
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,260
Amen.

